---
number: 171
title: Hark! Salvation News Is Sounding
author: Anonymous
composer: Unknown
sp_category: "15"
topic: The Christian Refuge
---

[verse 1]
Hark! Salvation news is sounding,
Christ has suffered on the tree;
Streams of mercy are abounding,
Grace for all is rich and free.

[verse 2]
Now, poor sinner,
Now, poor sinner,
Now, poor sinner,
Turn to Him who died for thee,
Turn to Him who died for thee.

[verse 3]
Oh, escape to yonder mountain;
Refuge find in Him today!
Christ invites you to the Fountain,
Come and wash your sins away:

[verse 4]
Do not tarry,
Do not tarry,
Do not tarry,
Come to Jesus while you may,
Come to Jesus while you may.

[verse 5]
Grace is flowing like a river,
Millions there have been supplied;
Still it flows as fresh as ever
From the Saviour’s wounded side;

[verse 6]
None need perish,
None need perish,
None need perish,
All may live, for Christ hath died,
All may live, for Christ hath died.
